"AI in Japan—OpenAI’s Japan Economic Blueprint | OpenAI (https://openai.com/index/japan-economic-blueprint)\nciteturn2955view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://openai.com/index/japan-economic-blueprint\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://openai.com/index/japan-economic-blueprint/; Total lines: 163\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2:   * [Button: Research]\nL3:   * [Button: Products]\nL4:   * [Button: Business]\nL5:   * [Button: Developers]\nL6:   * [Button: Company]\nL7:   * cite1†Foundation(opens in a new window)†openaifoundation.org L8: \nL9: cite2†Try ChatGPT(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com [Button: Login]\nL10: \nL11: OpenAI\nL12: \nL13: October 22, 2025\nL14: \nL15: cite3†Company cite4†Global Affairs L16: # AI in Japan—OpenAI’s Japan Economic Blueprint\nL17: \nL18: The Blueprint outlines how Japan can harness AI to accelerate innovation, strengthen competitiveness, and drive sustainable, inclusive growth.\nL19: \nL20: cite5†ブループリントを読む(opens in a new window)†cdn.openai.com cite6†Read paper(opens in a new window)†cdn.openai.com L21: \nL22: Loading…\nL23: \nL24: Share\nL25: \nL26: Empowering Japan’s next chapter of growth\nL27:   * cite7†Empowering Japan’s next chapter of growth L28:   * cite8†Building an AI-enabled future across industries L29:   * cite9†Investing in Japan’s AI infrastructure L30:   * cite10†Shaping a human-centered AI model for the world L31:   * cite11†A shared commitment to prosperity L32: \nL33:   * cite7†Empowering Japan’s next chapter of growth L34:   * cite8†Building an AI-enabled future across industries L35:   * cite9†Investing in Japan’s AI infrastructure L36:   * cite10†Shaping a human-centered AI model for the world L37:   * cite11†A shared commitment to prosperity L38: OpenAI is releasing a new Economic Blueprint for Japan that outlines a policy framework that sets out how Japan can fully utilize the economic and social potential of AI. The Blueprint reflects OpenAI’s commitment to supporting Japan’s long-term prosperity and leadership in the AI era, working alongside policymakers, industry leaders, and researchers to ensure AI benefits every sector and every generation.\nL39: ## Empowering Japan’s next chapter of growth\nL40: \nL41: Japan stands at a historic inflection point. From the Meiji Restoration to the postwar economic miracle, Japan has repeatedly shown the world how bold innovation can transform society. Now, as AI becomes the defining technology of this century, Japan has a once-in-a-generation opportunity to lead again.\nL42: Independent analyses estimate that AI could add more than ¥100 trillion in economic value, raising Japan’s GDP by as much as 16%. The question is not whether Japan can succeed in this new era but how boldly it will seize the opportunity and the degree it emerges as a global AI leader.\nL43: \nL44: The Japan Economic Blueprint identifies three pillars for ensuring that AI becomes a driver of broad-based growth:\nL45:   1. Inclusive access to AI: Building a society where everyone from students and startups to SMEs and public institutions can participate in and benefit from AI innovation.\nL46: \nL47:   2. Strategic infrastructure investment: Accelerating the development of AI data centers, semiconductor manufacturing, and renewable energy networks to link the “watts and bits” that power AI.\nL48:   3. Education and lifelong learning: Empowering every generation to thrive in the AI economy through next-generation education and large-scale reskilling programs.\nL49: ## Building an AI-enabled future across industries\nL50: AI is already reshaping Japan’s economic foundation from manufacturing and healthcare to finance, education, and public services. In factories, AI is reducing inspection costs and optimizing workflows for thousands of small and midsize manufacturers. In healthcare and eldercare, it is helping professionals focus more time on people rather than paperwork, improving people’s lives and potentially saving trillions of yen in social costs.\nL51: In schools and universities, AI tutors like ChatGPT Edu are enhancing personalized learning and breaking language barriers for global research collaboration. And across local governments, from Saitama to Fukuoka, AI is improving public administration and citizen services.\nL52: These transformations represent more than efficiency gains, they point to a future in which Japan’s creativity, craftsmanship, and community values are amplified by technology.\nL53: ## Investing in Japan’s AI infrastructure\nL54: \nL55: Achieving these outcomes will require sustained national investment in both digital and physical infrastructure. Japan’s data-center market is projected to exceed ¥5 trillion by 2028, and energy demand will rise accordingly. The Blueprint calls for long-term coordination between government, industry, and academia to ensure that computing resources and green energy supply grow together—advancing both digital transformation (DX) and green transformation (GX).\nL56: ## Shaping a human-centered AI model for the world\nL57: \nL58: OpenAI believes Japan’s balanced approach to innovation, ethics, and inclusion can become a global model for the responsible use of AI. Japan’s flexible intellectual-property framework, high standards of trust, and investment in people position it uniquely to lead in defining fair, open, and human-centered AI governance.\nL59: ## A shared commitment to prosperity\nL60: \nL61: The Japan Economic Blueprint is a living document—one that will evolve as Japan’s AI ecosystem grows. It calls for collective action across sectors to ensure that innovation uplifts everyone, from large enterprises to small workshops, from urban centers to rural regions.\nL62: Just as Japan once rebuilt and reimagined its economy for the industrial age, it can now do the same for the age of intelligence. By investing in infrastructure, education, and open innovation, Japan can turn the promise of AI into shared prosperity for generations to come.\nL63: \nL64: The full Japan Economic Blueprint is available cite6†here⁠(opens in a new window)†cdn.openai.com .\nL65: \nL66:   * cite12†Global Affairs L67:   * cite13†2025 L68: ## Author\nL69: \nL70: OpenAI\nL71: ## Keep reading\nL72: \nL73: cite14†View all L74: \nL75: cite15†Helping small businesses put AI to work Global AffairsSep 30, 2026 L76: \nL77: cite16†DevDay 2026 Recap CompanySep 29, 2026 L78: \nL79: cite17†Introducing dots ProductSep 29, 2026 L80: \nL81: Research\nL82: \nL83:   * cite18†Research Index L84:   * cite19†Research Overview L85:   * cite20†Economic Research L86: \nL87: Latest Advancements\nL88: \nL89:   * cite21†GPT-6.1 L90:   * cite22†GPT-6 L91:   * cite23†GPT-5.6 L92:   * cite24†GPT-5.5 L93: \nL94: Safety\nL95:   * cite25†Safety Approach L96:   * cite26†Deployment Safety(opens in a new window)†deploymentsafety.openai.com L97:   * cite27†Security & Privacy L98:   * cite28†Trust & Transparency L99: \nL100: Products\nL101:   * cite2†ChatGPT(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L102:   * cite29†ChatGPT Business(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L103:   * cite30†ChatGPT Enterprise(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L104:   * cite31†ChatGPT for Education(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L105:   * cite32†Codex†chatgpt.com L106:   * cite33†Dots(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L107:   * cite34†Release Notes L108: \nL109: API Platform\nL110: \nL111:   * cite35†Overview L112:   * cite36†API Log In(opens in a new window)†platform.openai.com L113:   * cite37†Docs(opens in a new window)†developers.openai.com L114: \nL115: Business\nL116:   * cite38†Overview L117:   * cite39†Solutions L118:   * cite40†Resources L119:   * cite41†Plugins L120:   * cite42†Customer Stories L121:   * cite43†Partner Network L122:   * cite44†Contact Sales L123: \